is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: router4
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the inter-router uplink from Location C’s gateway (router4) to the core (RIP domain) is down. Specifically, router4’s eth5 interface toward router3 on 172.25.1.0/24 is down, so router4 is isolated.

Mechanism: PCs in 192.168.200.0/24 send traffic to Location A via their default gateway 192.168.200.1 (router4). Because router4 has no working path to the core, it immediately returns ICMP “Destination Net Unreachable,” which users observe as total loss to 172.16.10.x/20.x. Other zones still reach each other because the core (including router3) remains healthy.

Localization: 
- From pc11→pc4 (172.16.10.4): “From 192.168.200.1 Destination Net Unreachable.” 192.168.200.1 is router4.
- router4: ip link
